used to calculate the speed of sound. From the results, the proposed method produced good results in a wide range of parameters. Therefore, the results of our calculations, in this study, will be useful for different aspects of technology and industry. One of the advances of this study is the use of series formulas of the exponential functions for the established formulas of second virial coefficients. It is well known that the series formulas of the exponential functions are general and provide accurate results of arbitrary values of parameters. Therefore, the obtained formulas for the second virial coefficient and related quantities are valid in the arbitrary values of parameters. Note that the virial coefficients are applied at the specific pressure and temperature ranges that molecules show the gas characteristic. At low temperatures and high pressures, the gases begin to form liquids with great deviations from ideal behavior. As seen from the tables, at low temperatures and high pressures, the calculation results obtained from the second virial coefficient deviate.
IV. Conclusions
In this paper, an efficient approach is described for the analytical evaluation of the specific heat capacity and speed of sound, through use of the virial coefficient. Results for the specific heat capacity and speed of sound, for several different molecules, are reported and then compared with data from the literature.
